5. WHAT THE MODEL'S INPUTS TIE THE RESULT TO (read from the files)
   plane days (DRcalc): latitude 52.160, longitude 4.497, PVGIS-SARAH2 2005 to 2020: 50 of 50 planes
   the monthly mean that scales the day (v2/vendor/solar/pvgis-leiden-monthly-2015-2020.json): latitude 52.160, longitude 4.497, PVGIS-SARAH2 2015 to 2020;
     September 4.014 kWh/m2 a day on 40/0; the scale 1.007820 is it over the 40/0 DRcalc day's sum
   the lid basis 13.23 C: the minimum of the 40/0 DRcalc file's September T2m (energy_two_pack.py's DRCALC)
   the ratio 0.9417: energy_inputs.yaml solar.panel.performance_ratio, src "PVGIS PVcalc totals l_aoi, l_spec, l_tg, l_total (AI arithmetic); the low is this stream's bracket for the fixed-voltage penalty, INFERRED"
   Every day, the scale, the lid basis and the ratio come from that one site; no other site's file is in the tree,
   so no other site is run here.

END. Each line is the model's arithmetic on the September reference day; nothing is measured.
